Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: leave packet flow hashing to the stack

The FOE table index is needed by PPE, but is not always a packet flow
hash. Four host-directed UDP streams on XR1710G reported index 0x7fff
and CPU reason 7. All 35760 captured packets consequently received the
same jhash_1word() value, marked as an L4 hash. RPS then kept every flow
on one CPU even with a two-CPU receive mask.

Leave the skb hash unset so the stack can derive it from the packet.
Keep the descriptor index and PPE flow-learning hook unchanged.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -981,9 +981,9 @@ static int airoha_qdma_rx_process(struct airoha_queue *q, int budget)
 
 		msg1 = le32_to_cpu(READ_ONCE(desc->msg1));
 		hash = FIELD_GET(AIROHA_RXD4_FOE_ENTRY, msg1);
-		if (hash != AIROHA_RXD4_FOE_ENTRY)
-			skb_set_hash(q->skb, jhash_1word(hash, 0),
-				     PKT_HASH_TYPE_L4);
+		/* FOE slots can be shared by unrelated host-directed flows.
+		 * Let the stack compute the packet hash for receive steering.
+		 */
 
 		reason = FIELD_GET(AIROHA_RXD4_PPE_CPU_REASON, msg1);
 		if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED)
